# SOC Investigation KQL Queries

![KQL](https://img.shields.io/badge/language-KQL-blue)
![Microsoft Defender XDR](https://img.shields.io/badge/platform-Microsoft%20Defender%20XDR-0078D4)
![Use case](https://img.shields.io/badge/use%20case-SOC%20%7C%20Threat%20Hunting-success)

A collection of KQL queries for SOC investigations, threat hunting, malware analysis and incident response in **Microsoft Defender XDR** (Advanced Hunting).

Each query has a short **Purpose** line and uses `<PLACEHOLDER>` values, so it can be adapted to any environment. For the Splunk equivalents, see [SOC-Investigation-Splunk-Queries](https://github.com/Kamil-Czarniecki/SOC-Investigation-Splunk-Queries).

## How to use

- Replace every `<PLACEHOLDER>` with a real value before running the query.
- Run the queries in **Microsoft Defender portal → Hunting → Advanced hunting**.
- Always narrow the time range (e.g. `| where Timestamp > ago(7d)`) on large tenants to keep queries fast.
- Prefer `==` / `=~` (exact) or `has` (term match) over `contains` where possible; `contains` is slower.

